  <ym-title|Selected terminal birth and moment receipt:
  evidence><label|selected-terminal-birth-and-moment-receipt-evidence>

  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and source-correspondence
  review pending. Pinned source revision:
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The prose is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-birth-receipt.tex> and
  its main result is <verbatim|thm:ex-selected-birth-moment>. It records the
  selected public route from the terminal census birth polynomial to its
  finite-volume normalized mode moments. The exact backward integration and
  compactness argument are proved in the manuscript. The selected service,
  origin geometry, finite response price, and vacuum denominator estimates
  remain conditional inputs; this unit does not call them automatic
  consequences of the birth identity.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declarations /
  paths>>|<cell|<strong|Inspection notes>>>|<row|<cell|Terminal observable
  list and birth polynomial>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.item>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.birth>, <verbatim|.boot>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Badlands.lean>,
  <verbatim|Bungalow.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|item> is a signed-coordinate
  pull/translation of the selected physical cylinder. <verbatim|birth> is
  <verbatim|(R.eval U)> times the finite polynomial pass of the sum of marker
  sends. <verbatim|boot> gives the singleton fire coefficient; general mode
  extraction follows from the census pass/product
  identity.>>|<row|<cell|Compactness and terminal
  integrability>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.hatCont>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.generics>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occurs>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Glacier.lean>>|<cell|The representative
  evaluation is continuous by the selected Wilson start identity and
  continuity of the bare evaluation. Each pulled/moved observable is
  continuous by <verbatim|generics>. Since configuration space is compact,
  the finite birth polynomial is integrable against prior Haar. The proof
  does not claim continuity of arbitrary intermediate density
  fields.>>|<row|<cell|Public selected service and birth
  route>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Geyser.pond>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ponds.past>; <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occursT>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tentF>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Pond.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Placed.lean>,
  <verbatim|Tackle.lean>>|<cell|The public root-test proof <verbatim|tentF>
  calls <verbatim|occursT> with a <verbatim|Ponds> receipt, then applies the
  spacer inequality. <verbatim|Geyser.pond> converts the selected-history
  <verbatim|Geyser> input to <verbatim|Ponds>; <verbatim|Ponds.past>
  constructs each label's <verbatim|Nectar> service from
  <verbatim|Freightage>, <verbatim|Fiesta>, <verbatim|Cherry>,
  <verbatim|Banks>, Brine, and the selected geometry inputs. In
  <verbatim|occursT>, <verbatim|Frost.upper> supplies servedness at the
  reference scale, <verbatim|punctual> supplies finite response toll/activity
  bounds, and <verbatim|vista> performs finite Wilson moment transfer.
  <verbatim|Geyser.at> is a parallel service lemma, not the
  <verbatim|occursT> caller on this route.>>|<row|<cell|Backward density
  flow>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.Rank.Course.flow>, <verbatim|.flow_step>,
  <verbatim|.flow_int>, <verbatim|.flow_sum>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/RANK/Course.lean>>|<cell|Flow is a finite recursion
  by the selected probability push, without a physical cell-volume factor.
  <verbatim|flow_int> follows by induction from
  <verbatim|StepData.push_integrable>; <verbatim|flow_sum> follows from
  <verbatim|StepData.push_integral>. Both use the same selected history above
  the reference.>>|<row|<cell|Slice and product
  integrability>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.RG.StepData.push_slice>,
  <verbatim|.push_integrand>, <verbatim|.push_integrable>,
  <verbatim|.push_integral>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG/Push.lean>>|<cell|A lawful
  transition has bounded density; each fixed coarse slice is integrable, and
  the full product integrand is integrable. This is the precise source
  property used to pass integrability through each finite push and to commute
  finite-dimensional coefficient extraction with integration. Finite total
  mass alone is not used as a pointwise slice claim.>>|<row|<cell|Finite
  response and origin price>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.punctual>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.scratch>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Traps.lean>,
  <verbatim|Maid.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|scratch> bounds the indexed scalar
  coefficient by three times the paid coefficient norm and the total tone
  charge by that norm. <verbatim|punctual> multiplies by positive marker
  weights and packages these as the two response budgets <verbatim|3a> and
  <verbatim|a> when every weighted paid size is at most <verbatim|a>. The
  geometric assumptions required for the whole mode are supplied by
  migration, occupancy and separated-origin inputs.>>|<row|<cell|Local
  density price and vacuum normalization>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.hove>,
  <verbatim|.sail>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Arbol.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|hove>
  gives the pointwise toll-weighted local density estimate from Served,
  Lawful, nonnegative coupling, Vault, and the response budgets.
  <verbatim|sail> integrates a fixed mode coefficient and uses the vacuum
  denominator lower bound. The monograph states these pointwise service and
  denominator estimates as explicit conditional hypotheses and proves
  cancellation of their common scalar.>>|<row|<cell|Final mode-moment
  estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.vista>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.occursT>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Arbol.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Placed.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|vista>
  iterates coefficient extraction through finite backward flow. At the
  terminal scale, the mode coefficient integrates to the Wilson partition
  function times the normalized moment. The scale-<math|k> local estimate
  plus vacuum treasury gives exponent <verbatim|\|Sites_k\| * Vac.treasury(k)
  + \|V\| * 6>; the six is <verbatim|3a+a+2f> with
  <verbatim|a=fly(k)\<leq\>1> and reserve <verbatim|f=1>. <verbatim|occursT>
  uses Ponds service; public <verbatim|tentF> applies the result to its
  selected observables.>>>>>

  <section|Checks and limits><label|checks-and-limits>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read the exact declarations and immediate dependencies in the
    table; no Lean source edits or Lean build were made.

    <item>No literature citation is needed for this finite source-specific
    passage.

    <item>The temporary wrapper <verbatim|/tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>
    includes this chapter. <verbatim|latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode
    -halt-on-error -outdir=/tmp/ym-centered-fragment-build
    /tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex> succeeded and produced a 36-page PDF.
    Eleven references remain unresolved because the wrapper omits OPE,
    lattice rate/step, and column-subpower units. Pages 33\U36 were rendered
    and inspected. <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> fails
    because the shared parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>
    is absent in this worktree; it was not created here.

    <item>No Lean build or tests were run, and no Lean source was changed.

    <item>The remaining substantive producer obligations are: the selected
    <verbatim|Geyser> and terminal <verbatim|Freightage> inputs; uniform
    migration/occupancy/Drake geometry; weighted paid-size bounds; and the
    local response/vacuum price package used by <verbatim|punctual>,
    <verbatim|hove>, and <verbatim|sail>. The manuscript has deliberately not
    replaced these with the names of their receipt fields.
  </itemize-minus>

